Description: Microsoft Surface Dial support: radial menu, tools, app profiles
 OpenDial turns the Microsoft Surface Dial into a programmable controller on
 Linux. Press and hold for a radial tool menu; turn to change volume, scroll,
 zoom, undo, brightness and media, or define tools with separate clockwise,
 counter-clockwise and click actions. Per-app profiles follow the focused
 window on GNOME, KDE, wlroots compositors and X11; haptic feedback,
 sensitivity and handedness are configurable.
 .
 The service runs as the logged-in user. A udev rule grants the active seat
 access to the Surface Dial only; no other input device is affected.
